  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Niki Lauda treated the development of a racing car as part of the driver's job. At Ferrari, his precise technical feedback and unsparing assessments helped turn an uncompetitive car into a winning machine. He carried that analytical approach to McLaren, where he beat his younger team-mate Alain Prost to the title by half a point.\n\nAs Mercedes' non-executive chairman, Lauda applied his judgement to people as well as machinery. He helped persuade Lewis Hamilton to join the team before its period of dominance, working alongside Toto Wolff. After Lauda's death in 2019, Mercedes made a red star on its cars a permanent tribute to him.",
